$NetBSD$

Add the NetBSD arm of a select() that has one arm per system.

Without an entry the default arm is taken, which is the Linux one.

--- tools/jdk/BUILD.tools.orig
+++ tools/jdk/BUILD.tools
@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@
     "jni_md_header-darwin",
     "jni_md_header-freebsd",
     "jni_md_header-linux",
+    "jni_md_header-netbsd",
     "jni_md_header-openbsd",
     "jni_md_header-windows",
     "platformclasspath",
